From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:47:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] memory: raise the zram swap capacity to 100% of RAM

memory: raise the zram swap capacity to 80% of RAM

Secure app spawning makes every app process about 43 MB larger and not
shareable with the zygote. With the stock 50% the swap is full about 30 s
after unlock and lmkd kills apps. zram is compressed RAM used only when
filled, so the limit costs no memory until needed, and the flash writeback
ceiling does not grow with it.

The stock value is removed from sysprop-inclusion.yml because a second
assignment with a different value fails post_process_props.py.

memory: raise the zram swap capacity from 80% to 100% of RAM

lmkd treats free swap below 10% of the total as low and then kills apps
when memory is short, so only 90% of the capacity is usable. On a lynx
with the same load of 4 GB of cold swap, 80% was below that line 55% of
the time and 100% never, with the same physical zram (1405 MB against
1452 MB). The stock 50% was below it all the time. zram is compressed RAM
used only when filled, so the larger limit costs no memory until needed.
---
 config/device/common/sysprop-inclusion.yml       |  2 --
 config/mk/google_devices/common/device-common.mk | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/config/device/common/sysprop-inclusion.yml b/config/device/common/sysprop-inclusion.yml
index b01fc41..ab73e1e 100644
--- a/config/device/common/sysprop-inclusion.yml
+++ b/config/device/common/sysprop-inclusion.yml
@@ -139,8 +139,6 @@ sysprop_inclusions:
   - mmd.zram.comp_algorithm = lz4
   - mmd.zram.comp_algorithm = lz77eh
   - mmd.zram.enabled = true
-  - mmd.zram.size = 3221225472
-  - mmd.zram.size = 50%
   - mmd.zram.writeback.device_size = 1073741824
   - mmd.zram.writeback.device_size = 2147483648
   - mmd.zram.writeback.enabled = true
diff --git a/config/mk/google_devices/common/device-common.mk b/config/mk/google_devices/common/device-common.mk
--- a/config/mk/google_devices/common/device-common.mk
+++ b/config/mk/google_devices/common/device-common.mk
@@ -84,3 +84,18 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES_DEBUG += \
     AirPodsDebugHarness \
     AirPodsProbeNoPerm \
     AirPodsProbeBtPriv
+
+# ObliviOS: zram swap capacity of 100% of RAM instead of the stock 50% (ADR-150).
+# Secure app spawning makes every app process about 43 MB larger and not shareable with
+# the zygote, so with 50% the swap is full about 30 s after unlock and lmkd kills apps.
+# zram is compressed RAM that is used only when filled (about 4.5x measured), so the
+# raise costs no memory until it is needed. The flash writeback ceiling does not grow
+# with it: mmd's idle writeback limit scales with used/total zram and is capped by
+# mmd.zram.writeback.max_bytes and device_size. The stock value is dropped from
+# sysprop-inclusion.yml because a second assignment with a different value fails
+# post_process_props.py. Kept in the common file like AirPods.
+# 100% and not 80%: lmkd treats free swap below 10% of the total as low, which is 90% of the
+# capacity usable. With a cold swap demand of 4 GB on top of the apps, 80% sat below that line
+# 55% of the time and 100% never, at the same physical zram (docs/research/
+# stallion-memory-pressure-investigation.md, "Zram capacity").
+PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += mmd.zram.size=100%
-- 
2.56.0

